    "result_text": "The suite contains a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create AUDIT line now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, with the previously-logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`) still present.\n\nThe edit was confined to the single `AUDIT.info(...)` statement in `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:132`):\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n    org.springframework.samples.petclinic.service.MembershipLevel.of(owner),\n    owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100));\n```\n\nStructural-impact choices:\n- **One file touched** (multiplier = 1) \u2014 computed the two new fields inline from the same formulas the `OwnerMapper` uses for the DTO, so the values match exactly what the test derives from the fetched owner.\n- **No new branches** \u2014 `addOwner`'s cyclomatic complexity is unchanged; only a logging call's arguments were extended.\n- **No new method or class**, avoiding paying the class's large `WMC_other` a second time, and no new import (fully-qualified reference, matching the existing codebase style in the mapper).\n\nThe verified log line: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`, and the suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
